  "descriptionShort": "Bilateral allocable [ODA](#dod:oda) that targets climate change mitigation, adaptation, or both, as a share of bilateral allocable ODA. Monetary aid is estimated as commitments.",
  "descriptionProcessing": "We combined the mitigation and adaptation markers of each project to count it only once. Projects marked as targeting both objectives (as a principal or significant objective) are counted as \"mitigation and adaptation\", and the others as \"mitigation only\" or \"adaptation only\". Projects with climate as the principal objective are those marked as principal for mitigation or adaptation; the remaining climate-related projects have climate as a significant objective.\n\nWe calculated this indicator by dividing climate-related ODA by bilateral allocable ODA, expressed as a percentage.\n\nWe calculated aggregates for groups of recipients (such as regions or income groups) by summing the indicator across the recipients that the OECD currently includes in each group. For income groups, this applies the most recent classification to all years.\n\nWe left out aid from the European Investment Bank (EIB), one of the EU institutions, as the OECD does in its own climate-related shares. The EIB tracks its climate finance with a different method, not with the Rio markers, so all its aid would otherwise count as non-climate aid.",
  "type": "float",
